<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Settings xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <Description_ENG>Auto-extracted schema for AI.ini. Descriptions come from the INI file's own ; comments. Generated by ja2-launcher/tools/build_ini_schemas.py.</Description_ENG>
    <Sections>
        <Section name="Modularized Tactical AI">
            <Properties>
                <Property name="NumFactories" datatype="numeric" defaultvalue="11">
                    <Description_ENG>DO NOT, repeat NOT add 'comments', spaces, or other stuff after the factory
names. The ini reader doesn't separate it from the data string.
Factory_n is used for any npc with bAIIndex set to n. Currently, the index is
copied from bTeam; I hope that somebody can integrate it into the map editor
soon. Then you can add any number of indices (up to 65535, that is), but they
must be consecutive.
Currently implemented factories:
NullPlanFactory - makes an NPC do absolutely nothing
LegacyAIPlanFactory - makes an NPC behave &quot;as before&quot;
Increase NumFactories accordingly</Description_ENG>
                </Property>
                <Property name="Factory_0" datatype="string" defaultvalue="NullPlanFactory">
                    <Description_ENG>not used</Description_ENG>
                </Property>
                <Property name="Factory_1" datatype="string" defaultvalue="LegacyAIPlanFactory">
                    <Description_ENG>'OUR_TEAM', so not really used either (?)</Description_ENG>
                </Property>
